From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:28:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: Renaming a file takes DELETE access.

As [MS-FSA] 2.1.5.15.12 and the SetFileInformationByHandle test have it:
renaming through a handle opened without DELETE fails with
STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED.  The server took any handle; making a new link to
the file still takes none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/tests/file.c b/dlls/kernel32/tests/file.c
index 67d33b8b8e5..d72135f471a 100644
--- a/dlls/kernel32/tests/file.c
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/tests/file.c
@@ -6259,7 +6259,6 @@ static void test_SetFileRenameInfo(void)
     fri->FileNameLength = wcslen(tempFileTo1) * sizeof(WCHAR);
     memcpy(fri->FileName, tempFileTo1, fri->FileNameLength + sizeof(WCHAR));
     ret = pSetFileInformationByHandle(file, FileRenameInfo, fri, size);
-    todo_wine
     ok(!ret && GetLastError() == ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, "FileRenameInfo unexpected result %ld\n", GetLastError());
     CloseHandle(file);
 
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index d89f775d52d..c334c17f008 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -3496,7 +3496,8 @@ DECL_HANDLER(set_fd_name_info)
         if (!root_fd) return;
     }
 
-    if ((fd = get_handle_fd_obj( current->process, req->handle, 0 )))
+    /* renaming takes DELETE, a new link to the file nothing */
+    if ((fd = get_handle_fd_obj( current->process, req->handle, req->link ? 0 : DELETE )))
     {
         set_fd_name( fd, root_fd, (const char *)get_req_data() + req->namelen,
                      get_req_data_size() - req->namelen, nt_name, req->link, req->flags );
